From 0adde9f4818bce16c22382d2bb5254cfe484d8b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:18:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Talk T8a: the house Talk mode HM_TALK on native (enter,
 gather, seats, camera, bubbles, talk_dm driven)

home_talk.c (inside DOOMO_HAS_TALK: native only until TKP, so the GBA, PS1 and DC builds do not link it):
START > Talk or A next to a housemate in Live mode (320x240 only); everyone present joins and is the
audience (an adult is dropped before a child or the pet when the room is over full), gathers in 12-20
frames (largest seat cluster, else a half circle round a table or the middle; the player takes a spare
seat or the open side), the camera frames the group (zoom 2 + focus circle + a pan for the unscaled
reference renderer; view from the seats' fronts; at most one move in 45 frames), bubbles at the speakers'
heads through plat_room_project (3x26, typewriter and babble, previous bubble faded and shrunk, player's
line bottom left), talk_dm_say / _step / _tick / _end, B leaves, control card and one instruction line,
five starters until T8c. room_ref.c is unchanged (the T0 contract and the Dreamcast port rely on zoom 2
being ignored there). Runner: talk-enter, talk-say, talk-wait, talk-leave, expect-talk, family-add,
frame-time. run_scripts.sh reads "# resolutions:". Script home_talk_basic, test_home_talk.c (17 tests).

Pixels: only the START menu of a house or visit with someone in it gains a Talk row (native 320x240);
the other 100 scripts at both sizes hash identical frame for frame against origin 4303597.
GBA: .text / .data / .bss / .iwram byte for byte equal (nm -S names and sizes equal, home_draw.o code equal).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
